{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_101","type":"agent_message","text":"{\n  \"policy_name\": \"observed-candidate-33\",\n  \"method_summary\": \"Improved relative CPU time to 0.474 (score 0.556) from previous best of ~0.508. Core optimizations: 3D bmm throughout with reshaped (BH, L, D) tensors replacing 4D matmul; inv_sqrt_d fused into q instead of the larger logits tensor; Gram matrix computed via torch.bmm(x, x.transpose(1,2)) for a faster BLAS path compared to @; Gram tiling via unsqueeze+expand+reshape; fused p1_logits mul+add_ chain; late v-projection for cache locality; aggressive in-place elementwise ops (mul_, add_, sqrt_, clamp_, div_); pre-resolved weight reshapes to reduce tensor overhead. All 5 seeds pass quality gates.\",\n  \"next_direction\": \"Try computing q,k projections via per-head bmm (H small batches of (L,C)@(C,D)) versus one big (BL,C)@(C,HD) matmul, and investigate MKLDNN-friendly weight layouts for the linear projections.\"\n}"}}
